            <ArticleTitle>[Value of studying pain in objective assessment of the clinical status of patients after spinal surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author demonstrates the role of algologic studies (projective Stewart's test scale), scales of verbal and visual analogs) in objective evaluation of the clinical status of patients who underwent spinal surgery for lumbar pains. Differences have been revealed in the algologic status of patients who suffered restricted interventions and complex decompression stabilizing operations with posterior spondylodesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
